      "traceTextDiagram": "Hook Dispatch Processing\n├── hooks_dispatch/main.go entrypoint \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/hooks_dispatch/main.go:25\n│   ├── LoadConfigWithDefaults() \u003c-- 1a\n│   ├── NewDispatcherWithRegistry() \u003c-- 1b\n│   └── dispatcher.Dispatch() \u003c-- 1c\n└── Dispatcher execution flow \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/hooks/dispatcher.go:122\n    ├── HooksForEvent() lookup \u003c-- 1d\n    ├── runner.Run() execution \u003c-- 1e\n    └── Merge() combine results \u003c-- 1f",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nThe hook dispatch system solves the problem of **enforcing organizational policies and coordination** across multi-agent environments. Without this system, agents could modify files without task context, create edit conflicts, or bypass required workflows. The system provides a centralized way to intercept tool usage, validate operations against business rules, and coordinate shared resources through event-driven guards.\n\n## Details\n\nThe system operates through a **central dispatcher** that loads hook configurations from `hooks.yaml` files [1a]. When an agent attempts to use a tool, the dispatcher receives an event (like `PreToolUse`), finds matching hooks based on tool type, file paths, or actor context [1d], and executes them through either shell scripts or Go skills [1e]. \n\nThe dispatcher uses a **registry pattern** to route different hook types to appropriate runners [1b]. Each hook returns a decision (approve/block), optional context to inject, or actions to perform. The results are merged using deterministic rules where blocks override approvals [1f]. This enables use cases like:\n\n- **Task guards** that ensure active tasks exist before write operations\n- **File guards** that prevent edit conflicts through reservation systems  \n- **Context injection** that automatically adds relevant documentation\n- **Policy enforcement** that blocks prohibited operations\n\nThe system is designed to be **extensible and configurable**, allowing workspace-specific hook configurations while maintaining a stable execution contract across all hook skills [1c]."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "title": "Task Guard Enforcement",
      "description": "Ensures active task exists before allowing write operations in task-centric workflow",
