      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "Task Guard Enforcement Flow\n├── Check if write operation \u003c-- 2a\n├── Open SQLite task store \u003c-- 2b\n├── Ensure active task exists \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/tasks/store.go:551\n│   ├── Get existing active task \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/internal/storage/tasks/store.go:508\n│   └── Create new task if needed \u003c-- 2c\n├── Dirty task if reviewed \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/hooks_task_guard/main.go:90\n│   └── Demote status to in_progress \u003c-- 2d\n└── Create graph tracking edge \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/hooks_task_guard/main.go:193\n    └── Link task to modified file \u003c-- 2e",
      "traceGuide": "## Motivation\n\nIn multi-agent coding environments, **uncoordinated file modifications** create chaos. Without coordination, agents can overwrite each other's work, lose context about what they're working on, and create inconsistent states. The task guard solves this by enforcing a **task-centric model** where every write operation must be associated with an active task, providing traceability and preventing aimless modifications.\n\n## Details\n\nThe task guard intercepts all write operations [2a] and ensures they have proper task context. When a write is attempted, it first opens the SQLite task store [2b] to access workspace task state. The system then ensures an active task exists - either retrieving the current one or creating a new one with a sensible default title derived from the tool and file path [2c]. \n\nIf the task was previously marked as ready for review or completed, the guard automatically \"dirties\" it back to in_progress status [2d], acknowledging that new work is being done. Finally, it creates a graph edge linking the task to the modified file [2e], enabling PageRank-based importance calculations and maintaining a complete audit trail of what work touched which files.\n\nThe system operates in two modes: **auto mode** creates tasks automatically for seamless workflow, while **strict mode** blocks operations without explicit active tasks, enforcing stricter governance."
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "title": "File Guard Reservation System",
      "description": "Prevents edit conflicts through SQLite-backed file reservation system",
      "locations": [
