          "path": "/Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/hooks_file_guard/main.go",
          "lineNumber": 171,
          "lineContent": "if err := boardStore.Reserve(ctx, \u0026reservation); err != nil",
          "title": "Store Reservation",
          "description": "Persists reservation to prevent other agents from editing"
        }
      ],
      "traceTextDiagram": "File Guard Reservation System\n├── Filter write operations only \u003c-- 3a\n├── Open SQLite board store\n│   └── OpenBoardStore() for persistence \u003c-- 3b\n├── Check for existing conflicts\n│   └── CheckConflicts() query against DB \u003c-- 3c\n├── Handle conflict response\n│   ├── Block if strict mode \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/hooks_file_guard/main.go:122\n│   └── Warn if advisory mode \u003c-- /Users/jkatigbak/repos/personal/agentctl/skills/hooks_file_guard/main.go:137\n└── Create new reservation\n    ├── Build FileReservation struct \u003c-- 3d\n    └── Store in database\n        └── Reserve() insert record \u003c-- 3e",
      "traceGuide": "# Motivation\n\nIn multi-agent coding environments, **file conflicts** are a critical problem. When multiple agents work on the same codebase simultaneously, they can overwrite each other's changes, leading to lost work and unpredictable behavior. The File Guard system solves this by implementing an **adversarial file reservation system** that prevents concurrent edits to the same files, similar to how version control systems prevent conflicting commits, but operating in real-time during tool execution.\n\n# Details\n\nThe File Guard operates as a hook skill that intercepts **write operations** before they execute [3a]. When a write tool (like Edit, Write, or fs.write_*) is invoked, the guard first checks if the operation affects files by extracting paths from the tool input. It then opens a SQLite-backed board store for persistence [3b] and queries for existing reservations that would conflict with the requested operation [3c].\n\nThe conflict detection follows clear rules: **exclusive reservations** conflict with any other reservation, while **shared reservations** only conflict with exclusive ones. If conflicts are found, the guard can either **block** the operation entirely in strict mode or **warn** but allow it in advisory mode [3d]. When no conflicts exist, the guard creates a new reservation linked to the current task and actor, with a configurable TTL (default 10 minutes) [3e].\n\nThis system integrates with the broader task management workflow by associating file reservations with active tasks, providing traceability for who modified what and why. The reservation data includes the holder's identity, task context, reason for modification, and expiration time, enabling coordination between agents while maintaining isolation boundaries."
    }
  ],
  "description": "Codemap covering the hook dispatch and enforcement guard system that manages tool execution through event-driven hooks, task-centric workflows, and file conflict prevention. Key locations include the central dispatcher loading [1a] and executing hooks [1c], task guard ensuring active tasks before writes [2c], and file guard preventing conflicts through reservations [3c].",
